Tier 2 -- golden vectors (workstation, milliseconds).

The snapshot name is the wire protocol and two implementations consume it, so
neither is the oracle: a committed vector file is. Config parsing gets the same
treatment. Run twice, under LC_ALL=C and a UTF-8 locale, and under a non-UTC
TZ, because timestamps are UTC-always by spec. See TESTING.md §3.

Empty at M0 -- the milestone fence is scaffolding only, and the parsers this
tier tests are M1. tests/run.sh reports "tier 2: no tests", which is not a
failure.

Files named t_*.sh are tests; anything else here is ignored.
